comments.body:
Some actually useful attributes of a c=Chief of Staff:

1.  Expertise in the business (if the boss didn't grow up in the business);
2.  Team-building among executives;
3.  Sending the tough messages so the boss doesn't have to;
4.  Giving the boss tough love so the executive team doesn't have to;
5.  (Nice to have) Strong moral compass, with willingness to say "goodbye" to the job if the boss persists in making harmful decisions.

My guess is that FIFA does not have a Chief of Staff position.
